IMPORT prelude

-- Sentosa Development Corporation Act 1972 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person who owns property, builds, or takes a
-- boat out on Sentosa: building and marine-facility permits in the resort area and the cessation order (ss 20-22), the monthly
-- maintenance contribution on resort-area property, who must pay it and how the Corporation recovers it (ss 24, 25), the navigation
-- offences in the waters of Sentosa (ss 27, 28, 33), oral contracts with the Corporation (s 37(3)), composition (s 38) and the
-- ceiling on penalties in regulations (s 40(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on
-- 31 December 2021"), informal consolidation -- version in force from 1/11/2022, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SDCA1972.txt. The latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 31 of 2022 wef 01/11/2022 (s 2 and
-- s 6). The deposit's metadata says it was the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0204 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a resident, property owner, builder or boat user actually meets. Not encoded:
-- the constitution, meetings and staff of the Corporation (ss 3-8), its functions and powers (ss 9, 10), vehicle permits and
-- charges (s 11 -- a pure discretion with no rule to test), finance (ss 13-18), the content of the cessation order (s 22(2)) and
-- the Corporation's self-help power (s 22(4), (6)), the Marina Superintendent's powers to give and enforce directions
-- (ss 26, 29-32, 34), the Registrar's documents on a sale (s 25(4)), regulations (s 40(1)) and the 1972 transfer (s 41).
-- The prescribed contribution rates and interest rates are in subsidiary legislation that was not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Sentosa Development Corporation Act 1972 -- resort area and waters`

§§ `20, 21 -- permits in the resort area`

-- s 20(1): "A person must not commence or carry out, or permit or authorise the commencement or carrying out of, any building works
-- affecting or changing the facade or external appearance of any building in the resort area unless there is in force a permit
-- granted by the Corporation". (2) the Corporation may refuse; (3) may impose conditions; (4) may cancel the permit for breach of a
-- condition.
-- s 21(1): the same for constructing or altering "any marine facility in the resort area".
-- s 19(1): the "resort area" is the part of Sentosa the Corporation designates by notice in the Gazette.
-- Works that leave the facade and external appearance alone need no s 20 permit, and nothing in Part 5 reaches a building outside
-- the resort area.
GIVEN `the works change the facade or external appearance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the building is in the resort area` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a building permit is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building works are an offence` IF
        `the works change the facade or external appearance`
    AND `the building is in the resort area`
    AND (NOT `a building permit is in force`)

GIVEN `the facility is in the resort area` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a marine facility permit is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the marine facility work is an offence` IF
        `the facility is in the resort area`
    AND (NOT `a marine facility permit is in force`)

§§ `20(5), 21(5), 22(5), 27, 28, 33, 40(2) -- maximum penalties`

-- ss 20(5), 21(5), 22(5): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both and, in the
-- case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $100 for every day during which the offence continues after
-- conviction". s 22(5): a person served with a cessation order who "fails to comply with the order".
-- s 27: navigating without due care and attention, or dangerously -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000".
-- s 28(1): owner or master of a vessel adrift -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000".
-- s 33(1): master failing to comply with a general or special direction -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000".
-- s 40(2): regulations "may impose a penalty not exceeding $2,000 for any breach thereof".
-- No imprisonment is provided for ss 27, 28, 33 or regulations; 0 below means the Act provides none.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `building works without a permit`
    `marine facility works without a permit`
    `ignoring a cessation order`
    `careless or dangerous navigation`
    `a vessel adrift`
    `ignoring a navigation direction`
    `breach of the regulations`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `ignoring a navigation direction` THEN 2000
    WHEN `breach of the regulations` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence carries a daily fine` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `building works without a permit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `marine facility works without a permit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ignoring a cessation order` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the offence carries a daily fine` `the offence`
    THEN `the base maximum fine` `the offence` PLUS 100 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
    ELSE `the base maximum fine` `the offence`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the offence carries a daily fine` `the offence` THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `38 -- composition`

-- s 38(1): the Corporation "may compound any offence under this Act or any regulations made under this Act by collecting from a
-- person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum not exceeding $500". (2) on payment no further proceedings.
-- The ceiling is the same for every offence, the $5,000 ones included.
GIVEN `the sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition sum is within the limit` IF
    `the sum` AT MOST 500

§§ `27, 28, 33 -- navigation in the waters of Sentosa`

-- s 27: "A master who navigates a vessel in the waters or waterways of Sentosa -- (a) without due care and attention; or (b) in a
-- manner liable to injure or endanger persons, other vessels, the marine facilities in Sentosa or any structure or installation in
-- Sentosa, shall be guilty of an offence".
GIVEN `without due care and attention` IS A BOOLEAN, `in an endangering manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the navigation is an offence` IF
    `without due care and attention` OR `in an endangering manner`

-- s 28(1): "The owner or master of a vessel adrift in the waters and waterways of Sentosa shall be guilty of an offence". (2) "It is a
-- defence ... to prove that the vessel did not become adrift as the result of any neglect or default on the part of the owner or
-- master." The burden of the defence is on the accused. s 2: "owner", for a vessel, "includes the charterer".
GIVEN `the vessel is adrift` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no neglect or default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vessel adrift is an offence` IF
    `the vessel is adrift` AND (NOT `proved no neglect or default`)

-- s 33(1): "The master of a vessel who fails to comply with a general or special direction shall be guilty of an offence". (2) a
-- defence "to prove that he or she had reasonable ground for supposing that compliance with the direction in question would be
-- likely to imperil the vessel or that in the circumstances compliance was impracticable".
GIVEN `failed to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved compliance would likely imperil the vessel` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved compliance was impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ignoring the direction is an offence` IF
        `failed to comply with the direction`
    AND (NOT `proved compliance would likely imperil the vessel`)
    AND (NOT `proved compliance was impracticable`)

§§ `24 -- the maintenance contribution`

-- s 24(1): "As from 1 November 1996, the Corporation may in each month levy a contribution at the prescribed rates in respect of all
-- immovable properties in the resort area". (2) payable by owners "quarterly in advance, without demand". (3)(a) "in addition to
-- any property tax"; (b) recoverable as a debt; (c) "if not paid within 30 days when they became due and payable, bear interest at
-- the prescribed rates".
-- Days are counted from the date the contribution fell due. Paid on day 30 or earlier -- no interest.
GIVEN `days unpaid after falling due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `interest runs on the contribution` IF
    `days unpaid after falling due` GREATER THAN 30

-- s 24(4): "the owner of the immovable property is liable, jointly and severally with any person who was liable to pay the same when
-- the contributions became due and payable". So the present owner answers for arrears run up by a predecessor.
-- s 24(5): "A person who has ceased to be the owner ... is only liable to pay (a) the contributions which were unpaid at the time the
-- person ceased to be the owner ... and (b) the interest accruing on the unpaid contributions until the time they are paid."
-- s 24(6): "where a mortgagee is in possession ... the mortgagee is liable jointly and severally with the owner".
-- s 19(1): "owner" is the person receiving the rent (or who would receive it if let), and the person in the Valuation List. A tenant
-- who pays rent and does not receive it is not an "owner" (an inference from the definition; the text names no duty on tenants).
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the present owner, for its own arrears`
    `the present owner, for arrears that fell due under the previous owner`
    `a former owner, for arrears unpaid when it ceased to own`
    `a former owner, for contributions falling due after it ceased to own`
    `a mortgagee in possession`
    `a mortgagee not in possession`
    `a tenant paying rent`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is liable for the contribution` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the present owner, for its own arrears` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the present owner, for arrears that fell due under the previous owner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a former owner, for arrears unpaid when it ceased to own` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a mortgagee in possession` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `25 -- the charge and the power of sale`

-- s 25(1): where contributions and interest "remain unpaid at the end of 90 days after the Corporation has served on the owner ... a
-- written demand", they "constitute a charge on the immovable property upon lodgment of an instrument of charge by the Corporation
-- with, and the registration of the instrument by, the Registrar".
-- "At the end of 90 days" is read as: 90 or more days have run since the demand was served (an interpretation).
GIVEN `days since the written demand` IS A NUMBER,
      `still unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the instrument of charge is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrears are a charge on the property` IF
        `days since the written demand` AT LEAST 90
    AND `still unpaid`
    AND `the instrument of charge is registered`

-- s 25(3): the Corporation "must not exercise its power of sale ... unless (a) a resolution has been passed by the Corporation to
-- have the immovable property sold; (b) a notice of the intended sale approved by the Registrar has been published once in one or
-- more daily newspapers ...; (c) during the period of 6 weeks after the date of the publication ... no payment has been received
-- for the contributions due including interest thereon and for the cost of publication as well as any other necessary incidental
-- charges; and (d) there is no legal action pending in court to restrain the Corporation".
-- 6 weeks is taken as 42 days, and the period must have run.
GIVEN `the charge is registered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a resolution to sell was passed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an approved notice was published` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since publication` IS A NUMBER,
      `payment was received after publication` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a court action to restrain the sale is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may sell the property` IF
        `the charge is registered`
    AND `a resolution to sell was passed`
    AND `an approved notice was published`
    AND `days since publication` AT LEAST 42
    AND (NOT `payment was received after publication`)
    AND (NOT `a court action to restrain the sale is pending`)

-- s 25(5): the owner "is, upon payment of the amount of contributions and interest and any necessary incidental charges owing to the
-- Corporation before it has exercised its power of sale ..., entitled to an instrument of discharge". (6) if the Corporation refuses,
-- a court order may discharge the property.
GIVEN `paid contributions, interest and incidental charges in full` IS A BOOLEAN, `the property has been sold` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is entitled to a discharge` IF
    `paid contributions, interest and incidental charges in full` AND (NOT `the property has been sold`)

§§ `37(3) -- oral contracts with the Corporation`

-- s 37(3): a contract that between private persons "would be valid although made orally, may be similarly made on behalf of the
-- Corporation ... but no oral contract may be made involving payment by the Corporation of a sum exceeding $500".
-- (1), (2): contracts needing a seal or signed writing between private persons need the Corporation's seal, or writing signed by the
-- Chief Executive or an authorised person.
GIVEN `valid orally between private persons` IS A BOOLEAN, `payment by the Corporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may contract orally` IF
    `valid orally between private persons` AND `payment by the Corporation` AT MOST 500
